# Fiji MCP — stdio and data paths

- The MCP server speaks **JSON-RPC on stdout**. ImageJ **`print()`** writes to stdout and **breaks** the session. Use **`return "...";`** (or equivalent) so metrics leave via the tool result, not the log stream.
- When **`FIJI_DATA_ROOTS`** is set on the server process, **`open_image`** and **`save_image`** paths must stay under one of those roots. Do not assume arbitrary filesystem access.
- Prefer **`FIJI_MODE=headless`** in Cursor unless GUI capture is required and a display is available.
- Set **`PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`** for the MCP subprocess in Cursor MCP JSON when possible.
